+# MedGuard Agent
 
-```markdown
-# MedGuard Agent: Zero-Trust Security Framework for Clinical AI
+A policy enforcement gateway that sits between an AI agent and clinical tools. Every tool call is authenticated, rate-limited, screened for prompt injection, authorised by Open Policy Agent, and executed with a single-use capability token bound to one user, one tool and one patient. Tool output is scrubbed for PHI before the agent sees it.
 
-**MedGuard Agent** is an open-source, production-grade security gateway and execution engine built to protect healthcare organizations from the unique vulnerabilities of **Agentic AI**.
+This is a working prototype against a mock patient store, not a deployed clinical system.
 
-While traditional web APIs rely on standard authentication (OAuth/JWT), AI agents introduce non-deterministic risks: prompt injections, unauthorized tool execution, cross-patient data exposure, and runaway API token consumption. MedGuard Agent sits between the client/user and underlying clinical tools, acting as a real-time **Policy Enforcement Point (PEP)** to guarantee zero-trust execution.
+## Request flow
 
+```mermaid
+flowchart LR
+  A[Agent / client] -->|X-API-Key| B[Authenticate<br/>identity from key, not body]
+  B --> C[Risk manager<br/>rate + token budget]
+  C --> D[Injection check<br/>NFKC normalise + deny-list]
+  D --> E[OPA / Rego<br/>assignment from record store]
+  E -->|allow| F[Mint single-use<br/>HMAC token]
+  F --> G[Tool verifies + consumes token]
+  G --> H[PHI redaction]
+  H --> I[Response]
+  B & C & D & E & G -.deny.-> L[(JSON audit log)]
+  H -.allow.-> L
 ```
 
----
+## Threat model and controls
 
-## 🎯 What This Project Solves
+| Threat | Control | Where | Test |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Caller claims to be the assigned doctor | Identity resolved from API key; patient assignment read server-side | `app/main.py` | `test_body_cannot_assert_identity` |
+| Policy engine outage turns into allow-all | Fails closed; bypass only with explicit `MEDGUARD_DEV_OPA_BYPASS=1` | `app/main.py` | `test_fail_closed_when_opa_unreachable` |
+| Stolen token replayed within its TTL | Random `jti` per token, consumed on first use | `app/security/capability.py` | `test_redteam_token_is_single_use` |
+| Token tampered to target another patient or tool | HMAC-SHA256 over exact payload bytes, scope re-checked | `app/security/capability.py` | `test_redteam_token_forgery_and_tampering` |
+| Prompt injection, including spacing / Unicode tricks | NFKC normalisation, zero-width stripping, regex deny-list; request blocked (400) | `app/security/sanitization.py` | `test_redteam_obfuscated_injection_detected` |
+| PHI leaking to the agent | Field redaction + pattern scrub of nested strings (SSN, email, phone, dates) | `app/security/sanitization.py` | `test_allowed_and_phi_redacted` |
+| Runaway agent loops / cost | Per-session velocity, call count and token budget | `app/security/risk.py` | `test_rate_limit` |
 
-Deploying AI models in clinical environments requires strict adherence to privacy (HIPAA/GDPR) and system isolation. MedGuard Agent solves three critical security challenges:
-
-1. **Prompt Injection & Jailbreaks:** Prevents malicious user prompts or external documents from overriding system instructions or coercing the agent into executing unauthorized tool calls.
-2. **Over-Privileged Tool Delegation:** Replaces broad API keys with single-use, cryptographically signed capability tokens that restrict an agent's execution to a specific patient, tool, and time window.
-3. **PHI Leaks & Session Abuse:** Scans outgoing tool outputs to redact Protected Health Information (PHI) and enforces hard rate/budget limits to prevent resource exhaustion.
-
